    <bpmn:process id="W_W486" name="W486. Related Party Transaction Disclosure &amp; Reporting (PAS 24)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly financial reporting cycle; year-end close (W9B); material related party transaction event
Frequency: Quarterly (disclosure schedule update); annual (PAS 24 note preparation for AFS)
Volume: 5 legal entities with extensive intercompany activity; ~20–30 material related party transactions/quarter
Owner: Controller
Participants: CFO, Tax Manager, Corporate Secretary, VP Legal, External Auditor
Source: workflow W486 — Related Party Transaction Disclosure &amp; Reporting (PAS 24)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W486_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W486_Lane1" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W486_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W486_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W486_Start4" name="Quarterly financial reporting cycle; year-end close (W9B); material related party…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task5" name="Related Party Register Maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Related Party Register Maintenance: Controller maintains the Related Party Register: (a) identify all related parties per PAS 24 definition: 5 legal entities, key management personnel (CEO, CFO, COO, CIO, CMO, CHRO, VP Legal, Board members), entities controlled or significantly influenced by key management personnel, associates and joint ventures; (b) classify relationships: parent-subsidiary, fellow subsidiaries, key management personnel, post-employment benefit plans; (c) update register for any changes (new board members, new related entities) quarterly
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task6" name="Transaction Capture &amp; Classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Transaction Capture &amp; Classification: Each quarter, Controller extracts all intercompany transactions from the ERP: (a) IC revenue and expense (W14 — intercompany logistics fees, ecommerce fees, leasing income); (b) IC receivables and payables balances; (c) IC loans and interest (W137); (d) IC guarantees and contingencies (W325); (e) IC dividends (W327); (f) management compensation and benefits per key management personnel (aggregated from payroll W10); (g) classify each transaction by related party, nature of relationship, and transaction type
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task7" name="Arm&#x27;s-Length Pricing Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Arm&#x27;s-Length Pricing Verification: Controller verifies that all material related party transactions are conducted at arm&#x27;s-length terms: (a) cross-reference transfer pricing documentation (W235) for goods and services; (b) verify IC leasing rates against market benchmarks (W275 — IFRS 16 disclosures); (c) verify IC service fees against SLA billing rates (W435); (d) flag any transactions where pricing deviates significantly from arm&#x27;s-length; (e) document justification for any non-arm&#x27;s-length terms
Responsible (R): Controller / Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task8" name="Quarterly Disclosure Schedule Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly Disclosure Schedule Update: Controller updates the Related Party Disclosure Schedule: (a) tabulate all material related party transactions by type, counterparty, and amount; (b) compute outstanding balances (receivable/payable) at quarter-end; (c) compute provisions for doubtful IC receivables; (d) compute management compensation per key management personnel category (short-term employee benefits, post-employment benefits, other long-term benefits, termination benefits — per PAS 19 categories)
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task9" name="PAS 24 Note Preparation (Annual)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: PAS 24 Note Preparation (Annual): For the annual AFS (W9B), Controller prepares the PAS 24 note: (a) describe the related party relationship nature; (b) disclose all material transaction types and amounts; (c) disclose outstanding balances and terms/conditions; (d) disclose provisions for doubtful IC receivables; (e) disclose key management personnel compensation (aggregated by category, not by individual — per PAS 24 paragraph 17); (f) disclose any guarantees provided or received; (g) ensure consistency with the W481 GIS beneficial-ownership/affiliate disclosures
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3–5 days/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task10" name="External Audit Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: External Audit Coordination: Controller coordinates with External Auditor on PAS 24 disclosures: (a) provide Related Party Register and Disclosure Schedule; (b) respond to auditor queries on specific transactions; (c) provide supporting documentation for arm&#x27;s-length pricing; (d) incorporate auditor feedback into final disclosure note
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): External Auditor
Duration: 2–3 days/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W486_Task11" name="Board Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Board Reporting: CFO presents related party transaction summary to Board (W124/W482): (a) quarterly: summary of material IC transactions; (b) annual: full PAS 24 disclosure note for Board approval before AFS filing (W481)
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): Board
Duration: Per W124</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W486_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W486_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W486_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W486_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W486_Assoc14" sourceRef="W486_Annotation13" targetRef="W486_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
