    <bpmn:process id="W_W487" name="W487. Revenue Recognition Review (PFRS 15 Complex Scenarios)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly financial close (W9A); year-end close (W9B); new revenue stream launch
Frequency: Quarterly (review); annual (comprehensive assessment)
Volume: ~10–15 complex revenue scenarios reviewed per quarter across 5 entities
Owner: Controller
Participants: CFO, VP Merchandising, VP Store Operations, COO, Tax Manager, External Auditor
Source: workflow W487 — Revenue Recognition Review (PFRS 15 Complex Scenarios)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W487_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W487_Lane1" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W487_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W487_Start3" name="Quarterly financial close (W9A); year-end close (W9B); new revenue stream launch">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task4" name="Revenue Stream Inventory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Revenue Stream Inventory: Controller maintains a register of all revenue streams requiring PFRS 15 assessment: (a) standard retail POS sales (straightforward — recognized at POS); (b) gift card sales and redemptions (W28); (c) loyalty points earning (W17); (d) bundled product + installation (W138); (e) consignment sell-through (W23); (f) layaway sales (W75); (g) subscription services (W282); (h) project-based sales with staged billing (W165); (i) vendor rebates and co-op advertising (W27, W153); (j) tool rental (W139); (k) marketplace commissions (W180)
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task5" name="Performance Obligation Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Performance Obligation Assessment: For each complex revenue stream, Controller assesses: (a) identify distinct performance obligations in each arrangement; (b) determine standalone selling price allocation (SSP) for each obligation; (c) determine revenue recognition timing (at a point in time vs. over time); (d) document the accounting treatment and rationale per PFRS 15
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 days/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task6" name="Deferred Revenue Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Deferred Revenue Calculation: Each quarter, Controller calculates deferred revenue balances: (a) Gift cards: outstanding unredeemed gift card balance (W28); estimate breakage rate based on historical redemption patterns; recognize breakage revenue for gift cards where likelihood of redemption is remote (per PFRS 15 paragraph B43); (b) Loyalty points: calculate total outstanding loyalty points liability (W104); allocate transaction price to points earned; adjust deferred revenue for points expiration and forfeiture; (c) Layaway deposits: review outstanding layaway agreements (W75) where customer has paid deposit but not taken delivery; assess whether revenue should be recognized; (d) Subscription services: review deferred revenue from pre-paid service contracts (W282); recognize revenue over service delivery period
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task7" name="Bundle Allocation Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Bundle Allocation Review: Each quarter, Controller reviews bundled revenue allocations: (a) product + installation bundles: verify SSP allocation between product (recognized at delivery/POS) and installation service (recognized at installation completion); (b) promotional bundles (W13): verify that the bundle discount is allocated proportionally across all items; (c) tool rental + maintenance: separate rental revenue (over time) from maintenance revenue (as incurred)
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task8" name="Consignment Revenue Timing Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consignment Revenue Timing Verification: Each quarter, Controller verifies consignment revenue recognition: (a) confirm that consignment goods remain vendor-owned until sold (W23); (b) verify that revenue is recognized only at point of customer sale (not at store receipt); (c) reconcile consignment inventory balance (vendor-owned) with consignment revenue recognized; (d) verify consignment settlement timing matches sell-through reports
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task9" name="Journal Entry Posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Journal Entry Posting: Controller posts quarterly PFRS 15 adjustment journal entries: (a) gift card breakage revenue recognition; (b) loyalty points deferred revenue adjustment; (c) bundle SSP allocation corrections; (d) subscription deferred revenue amortization; (e) any revenue timing corrections identified during review; all entries posted during month-end close (W9A) with supporting schedules
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W487_Task10" name="Annual Comprehensive Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual Comprehensive Review: At year-end (W9B): (a) review all PFRS 15 accounting policies for continued appropriateness; (b) recalculate breakage rates, SSP allocations, and deferred revenue balances using full-year data; (c) coordinate with External Auditor on PFRS 15 audit approach and sampling; (d) prepare PFRS 15 disclosure note for AFS (including disaggregated revenue by nature, timing, and transfer point); (e) assess any new revenue streams launched during the year (e.g., new marketplace channels, new service offerings) for PFRS 15 treatment
Responsible (R): Controller / External Auditor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 5–7 days/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W487_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W487_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W487_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W487_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: Controller review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
