    <bpmn:process id="W_W768" name="W768. BIR VAT Refund Claim Processing &amp; Input VAT Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly VAT review identifies excess input VAT over output VAT; or annual VAT reconciliation per W590
Frequency: Quarterly review; annual or ad-hoc claim filing
Volume: 1-2 VAT refund claims per year per entity (primarily entities with significant imports but low domestic revenue — e.g., Logistics Inc. during early years)
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: Tax Accountant, Finance Manager, CFO, External Tax Counsel, BIR
Source: workflow W768 — BIR VAT Refund Claim Processing &amp; Input VAT Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W768_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W768_Lane1" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W768_Lane2" name="External Tax Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W768_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W768_Start4" name="Quarterly VAT review identifies excess input VAT over output VAT; or annual VAT…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task5" name="Excess input VAT identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Excess input VAT identification: Tax Accountant reviews quarterly VAT reconciliation per W590: (a) input VAT from purchases (domestic and import per FIN-006), (b) output VAT from sales, (c) net VAT position; if excess input VAT &gt; PHP 1M, evaluates claim feasibility
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task6" name="Claim feasibility assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Claim feasibility assessment: Tax Accountant assesses: (a) expected BIR processing time (historical 6-24 months), (b) probability of approval (BIR audit history, documentation strength), (c) alternative: carry forward to offset future output VAT vs. claim cash refund, (d) cost of external tax counsel for claim preparation (~PHP 200-500K per claim)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task7" name="Documentation package preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Documentation package preparation: If proceeding with claim: Tax Accountant compiles BIR-required documentation: (a) BIR Form 2550M/Q showing excess input VAT, (b) schedule of input VAT claimed with supporting invoices/customs declarations, (c) proof of payment (bank receipts, customs payment receipts), (d) certificate of registration per REG-001, (e) sworn statement declaring no pending tax liabilities
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): External Tax Counsel
Duration: 20-40 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task8" name="External tax counsel review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: External tax counsel review: External tax counsel reviews documentation package for completeness and legal sufficiency; advises on claim strategy; prepares cover letter and legal memorandum supporting the refund claim
Responsible (R): External Tax Counsel
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8-16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task9" name="BIR claim submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: BIR claim submission: Tax Accountant files claim with BIR Revenue District Office (RDO) where entity is registered per REG-001: (a) submits complete documentation package, (b) obtains BIR acknowledgment receipt with tracking number, (c) enters claim in BIR tracking log
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task10" name="BIR follow-up and audit coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: BIR follow-up and audit coordination: During BIR processing: (a) monthly follow-up with BIR RDO on claim status, (b) prepare for BIR audit of claimed input VAT — provide original invoices, customs declarations, and payment proofs on demand, (c) coordinate with External Tax Counsel for BIR queries
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2-4 hours/month during processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task11" name="Claim resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Claim resolution: Upon BIR decision: (a) if approved: Tax Accountant records refund (DR Cash / CR Input VAT) or tax credit memo; (b) if partially approved: analyze disallowed amounts, adjust, and record net refund; (c) if denied: External Tax Counsel evaluates appeal via Court of Tax Appeals within 30 days
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W768_Task12" name="Quarterly VAT refund tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly VAT refund tracking: Tax Accountant maintains VAT refund tracking dashboard: (a) outstanding claims by entity and amount, (b) days since filing, (c) BIR audit status, (d) historical approval rate, (e) total input VAT carried forward vs. claimed
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1 hour/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W768_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W768_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W768_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W768_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: Tax Accountant review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
