    <bpmn:process id="W_W770" name="W770. AP Vendor Debit Memo Processing &amp; Account Deduction Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor quality issue, pricing discrepancy, or contract compliance violation identified
Frequency: Weekly; ~30–50 debit memos per month
Volume: ~30–50 debit memos per month (~PHP 5-15M in deductions)
Owner: AP Accountant
Participants: AP Accountant, Procurement Analyst, Finance Manager, Vendor
Source: workflow W770 — AP Vendor Debit Memo Processing &amp; Account Deduction Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W770_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W770_Lane1" name="AP Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W770_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W770_Lane3" name="Procurement Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W770_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W770_Start5" name="Vendor quality issue, pricing discrepancy, or contract compliance violation identified">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W770_Task6" name="Debit memo trigger identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Debit memo trigger identification: AP Accountant or Procurement Analyst identifies debit memo trigger: (a) quality hold — vendor defect per W110 requiring chargeback, (b) pricing discrepancy — vendor invoice exceeds contract price per W669, (c) short-shipment — goods received quantity &lt; invoiced quantity per W7, (d) transit damage — carrier damage claim with vendor responsibility per W500, (e) promotional rebate shortfall — vendor did not fund agreed promotional support per W513
Responsible (R): AP Accountant / Procurement
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W770_Task7" name="Documentation and evidence compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Documentation and evidence compilation: AP Accountant compiles supporting documentation: (a) original invoice and PO reference, (b) goods receipt discrepancy report, (c) quality inspection report per W681, (d) photo evidence of damage, (e) contract pricing schedule per W669, (f) communication log with vendor
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15-30 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W770_Task8" name="Debit memo creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Debit memo creation: AP Accountant creates debit memo in AP module: (a) references original invoice, (b) specifies deduction amount with calculation detail, (c) links supporting documentation, (d) selects deduction type (quality, pricing, shortage, damage, promotional), (e) applies against vendor AP balance
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 10 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W770_Task9" name="Vendor notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Vendor notification: System notifies vendor of debit memo via vendor portal (W705): (a) debit memo details and supporting documentation, (b) vendor response deadline (14 business days), (c) dispute mechanism if vendor disagrees
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W770_Task10" name="Vendor response management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Vendor response management: (a) If vendor accepts: debit memo finalized; AP balance reduced; deduction reflected in next payment run per W556. (b) If vendor disputes: Procurement Analyst engages vendor per W244 invoice dispute resolution; negotiate resolution; adjust debit memo if warranted; document agreed resolution. (c) If no response within 14 days: debit memo auto-finalized per terms
Responsible (R): Procurement Analyst / AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1-4 hours/dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W770_Task11" name="Settlement and reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Settlement and reconciliation: Debit memo settled through: (a) deduction from next payment to vendor per W556, (b) offset against vendor credit memo if vendor issues one, (c) separate wire transfer if vendor disputes and partial resolution reached
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W770_Task12" name="Monthly debit memo analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly debit memo analytics: AP Accountant reports: (a) debit memo volume by type, vendor, and category, (b) vendor acceptance vs. dispute rate, (c) average time to resolution, (d) total deductions as % of total AP, (e) top 10 vendors by debit memo frequency (indicating systemic issues requiring W110 CAPA)
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W770_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W770_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W770_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W770_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: must enforce one-to-one matching; operational: clear contract language per W688 CLM (preventive)
Owner: AP Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
