    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W813" name="W813. AP Vendor Invoice Duplicate Detection &amp; Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: System auto-detects potential duplicate vendor invoice during AP invoice entry per W7
Frequency: Daily; ~15–25 potential duplicates flagged per month
Volume: ~15–25 potential duplicates/month out of ~9,500 total invoices; ~60% are true duplicates
Owner: AP Accountant
Participants: AP Accountant, Finance Manager, Vendor
Source: workflow W813 — AP Vendor Invoice Duplicate Detection &amp; Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W813_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W813_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W813_Lane2" name="AP Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W813_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W813_Start4" name="System auto-detects potential duplicate vendor invoice during AP invoice entry per W7">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W813_Task5" name="Automated duplicate detection during invoice entry">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated duplicate detection during invoice entry: During AP invoice entry per W7, system automatically checks new invoice against existing invoices in the AP module using multi-criteria matching: (a) exact match: same vendor ID + same invoice number + same invoice amount — automatic hard block, (b) high-probability match: same vendor ID + same invoice amount + invoice date within 7 days — flagged for review, (c) PO reference match: same PO number + same PO line number already matched to another invoice — flagged for review, (d) fuzzy match: same vendor ID + similar amount (within 5%) + same invoice date — flagged for review. System prevents posting of hard-blocked invoices and queues flagged invoices for AP Accountant review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W813_Task6" name="AP Accountant review of flagged potential duplicate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AP Accountant review of flagged potential duplicate: AP Accountant reviews each flagged invoice pair or group: (a) pull original invoice: verify vendor name, invoice number, invoice date, line items, PO reference, and goods receipt status per W7 three-way match, (b) check payment status: is original invoice already paid per W556 payment run? If yes, risk of duplicate payment is high, (c) verify goods receipt: were goods received twice per W2 goods receipting? If two separate GRs exist for same PO, invoices may be legitimate partial shipments, (d) compare line-level detail: are identical SKUs, quantities, and unit prices repeated? Or are line items different despite similar totals?
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10-15 min/review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W813_Task7" name="Confirmed duplicate — reject second invoice">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Confirmed duplicate — reject second invoice: If AP Accountant confirms the second invoice is a true duplicate: (a) reject invoice with duplicate reason code in AP module: system links rejected invoice to original paid/posted invoice, (b) add notation: &quot;Duplicate of invoice [number] dated [date], paid on [date] via payment run [reference]&quot;, (c) system updates vendor duplicate counter for analytics, (d) no vendor communication required for unpaid duplicate rejection
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/rejection</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W813_Task8" name="Not a duplicate — approve with override">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Not a duplicate — approve with override: If AP Accountant determines the flagged pair is not a true duplicate: (a) document reason for override: (i) different PO references — vendor issued separate invoices for separate POs that happen to have similar amounts, (ii) partial shipment — legitimate second invoice for remaining PO quantity, (iii) credit note re-invoice — vendor cancelled original invoice per mutual agreement and re-issued with corrected amounts, (iv) coincidental amount match — different goods/services that happen to total similar amount, (b) approve invoice with override notation in system, (c) override creates audit trail entry flagged for Finance Manager periodic review
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/override</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W813_Task9" name="Duplicate already paid — initiate recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Duplicate already paid — initiate recovery: If duplicate invoice was already paid before detection (e.g., both invoices processed in same batch, or detection triggered retroactively): (a) AP Accountant confirms duplicate payment: two payments to same vendor for same invoice reference, (b) initiate recovery per W244 vendor invoice dispute: contact vendor accounts receivable with evidence of duplicate payment, (c) request either: (i) vendor refund via wire transfer, (ii) vendor credit note applied against next payment per W556, (iii) offset against other open vendor invoices, (d) track recovery status in AP module until resolved
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30-60 min/recovery case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W813_Task10" name="Vendor notification of duplicate rejection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Vendor notification of duplicate rejection: For rejected duplicates where vendor may re-submit: (a) system generates automated vendor notification via W705 vendor self-service portal: &quot;Invoice [number] rejected — duplicate of invoice [original number] processed on [date]. Please do not resubmit.&quot;, (b) for vendors not using portal: AP Accountant sends email notification with duplicate reference, (c) for repeat offenders (&gt;3 duplicates in 6 months): Procurement Analyst addresses with vendor per W706 supplier performance scorecard
Responsible (R): System / AP Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated + 5 min/email</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W813_Task11" name="Monthly duplicate analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly duplicate analytics: AP Accountant prepares monthly duplicate detection analytics: (a) total potential duplicates flagged vs. confirmed duplicates — detection precision rate, (b) duplicate rate by vendor: top 10 vendors by duplicate frequency, (c) root cause analysis: vendor billing error, re-submission of paid invoice, PO-level duplicate, inter-entity duplicate, (d) recovery status: total duplicate overpayments identified, amount recovered, amount outstanding, (e) override analysis: number of overrides and reasons — are any patterns emerging that suggest detection rules need tuning?
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W813_Task12" name="Quarterly vendor duplicate rate review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly vendor duplicate rate review: Finance Manager and AP Accountant conduct quarterly review with top offenders: (a) meet with Procurement to discuss vendors with persistent duplicate billing (&gt;5 duplicates per quarter), (b) Procurement engages vendor accounts receivable contact to investigate root cause on vendor side — often indicates vendor ERP or billing system issue, (c) for systemic vendor issues: request vendor implement duplicate invoice controls on their side, (d) update vendor performance scorecard per W706 with duplicate billing metric, (e) adjust system detection rules if false positive rate exceeds 40% — tune matching thresholds
Responsible (R): AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W813_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W813_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W813_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W813_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: duplicate-detection thresholds (incl. fuzzy matching) tuned quarterly against false-positive rates, per step 8e
Owner: AP Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W813_Assoc15" sourceRef="W813_Annotation14" targetRef="W813_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
