    <bpmn:process id="W_W1504" name="W1504. Supplier Invoice Price Discrepancy Investigation, Debit Note Issuance &amp; Resolution Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Three-way match identifies a price discrepancy between PO unit price and supplier invoice unit price exceeding the tolerance threshold (PHP 50 or 2%, whichever is greater)
Frequency: ~200–400 price discrepancy incidents per month across all suppliers; ~3–8% of all invoices received have some price variance
Volume: ~5,000–8,000 invoices processed per month chain-wide; ~200–400 with price discrepancies requiring investigation
Owner: AP Associate
Participants: AP Associate, Merchandise Planner, Buyer, Vendor Account Manager, AP Manager
Source: workflow W1504 — Supplier Invoice Price Discrepancy Investigation, Debit Note Issuance &amp; Resolution Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1504_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1504_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1504_Lane2" name="AP Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1504_Lane3" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1504_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1504_Start5" name="Three-way match identifies a price discrepancy between PO unit price and supplier invoice…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1504_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1504_Task6" name="Automated price discrepancy detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated price discrepancy detection: During three-way match: (a) system compares invoice line item price to PO line item price; (b) if variance &gt; tolerance (PHP 50 or 2%, whichever greater): (i) invoice line flagged as &quot;Price Discrepancy&quot;; (ii) invoice held in AP queue — cannot be processed for payment until resolved; (iii) AP Associate notified with: PO number, SKU, PO price, invoiced price, quantity, and variance amount; (c) invoice remains in &quot;Disputed&quot; status with payment blocked
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1504_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1504_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1504_Task7" name="Root cause investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Root cause investigation: AP Associate investigates the discrepancy: (a) checks PO: is the PO price correct? Was the PO based on a valid price list, quotation, or promotional agreement?; (b) checks vendor communication: was there a price increase notification? Did the buyer authorize a price change?; (c) checks unit of measure: does the discrepancy disappear if invoice price is multiplied by pack size?; (d) checks promotional calendar: was the PO placed during a promotional period with special pricing?; (e) common outcomes: (i) vendor error — invoice at wrong price; (ii) PO outdated — vendor price increased but PO wasn&#x27;t updated; (iii) unit of measure mismatch — invoice is per piece, PO was per case; (iv) promotional price not applied — vendor forgot promotional terms
Responsible (R): AP Associate
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per discrepancy</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1504_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1504_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1504_Task8" name="Debit note issuance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Debit note issuance: For confirmed vendor errors (vendor overcharged): (a) AP Associate issues a debit note through the vendor portal: (i) references the disputed invoice number, PO number, and SKU; (ii) specifies the correct price per PO agreement; (iii) calculates the overcharge amount; (iv) requests credit note from vendor or deduction from next payment; (b) debit note automatically linked to the disputed invoice in the system; (c) vendor notified via portal + email; (d) debit note tracked in the &quot;Open Debit Notes&quot; aging report; (e) AP Associate follows up if vendor does not respond within 10 business days
Responsible (R): AP Associate
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per debit note</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1504_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1504_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1504_Task9" name="Resolution &amp; invoice release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Resolution &amp; invoice release: When vendor agrees to the debit note: (a) vendor issues credit note referencing the original invoice and debit note; (b) AP Associate matches credit note to the debit note in the system; (c) disputed invoice adjusted: (i) correct price applied; (ii) variance resolved; (d) invoice released from &quot;Disputed&quot; status to &quot;Approved for Payment&quot;; (e) payment processed in next scheduled payment run per PA-15.2; (f) if vendor disputes the debit note: (i) AP Associate escalates to Buyer for commercial resolution; (ii) Buyer negotiates with Vendor Account Manager; (iii) resolution options: vendor accepts debit note, partial compromise, or BuildRight absorbs the difference (if PO was genuinely outdated); (iv) AP Manager approves any write-off of the variance amount &gt; PHP 5,000
Responsible (R): AP Associate / Buyer
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: 10–20 min per resolution</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1504_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1504_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1504_Task10" name="Monthly discrepancy analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly discrepancy analytics: Monthly: (a) AP Manager reviews price discrepancy analytics: (i) total number of discrepancies by vendor; (ii) total financial impact (overcharges identified and recovered); (iii) average resolution time (days from detection to resolution); (iv) repeat offender vendors (same vendor &gt; 5 discrepancies/month); (b) repeat offenders escalated to Category Manager for vendor performance discussion per PA-03.3; (c) systemic issues identified: (i) if a specific product category has high discrepancy rates → price master may need updating; (ii) if a specific unit-of-measure conversion causes frequent errors → master data fix needed; (d) monthly report shared with CFO
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1504_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1504_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1504_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1504_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1504_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: AP Associate review and approval gate
Owner: AP Associate</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1504_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1504_Annotation12" targetRef="W1504_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1504_Flow14" sourceRef="W1504_Start5" targetRef="W1504_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1504_Flow15" sourceRef="W1504_Task6" targetRef="W1504_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1504_Flow16" sourceRef="W1504_Task7" targetRef="W1504_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1504_Flow17" sourceRef="W1504_Task8" targetRef="W1504_Task9" />
