    <bpmn:process id="W_W5510" name="W5510. Supplier Service-Fee Billing &amp; Account Deduction for Store-Rendered Services (Barcode Labels &amp; Promotional Collaterals)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Chargeable service event auto-logged at source — barcode/price-label print run, vendor-initiated barcode change, promotional-collateral production, source-tag re-application; (b) monthly supplier service-fee statement cycle ahead of the W556 payment calendar
Frequency: Continuous event logging; monthly statement + debit-memo cycle
Volume: ~1,500–3,000 chargeable events/month chain-wide (~55–60% new-item barcode/price labels beyond free allowance and vendor barcode changes; ~25–30% promotional collateral production; ~10–15% source-tag re-application for missed vendor tags), concentrated in ~150–300 of the ~800–1,000 active vendors (≈10 events per affected vendor-month); ~5–10% of statements attract a dispute (~10–25/month)
Owner: AP Accountant
Participants: AP Clerk, Category Manager, Store Operations Manager (first-line dispute), Auto-ID Lead (event sources), Marketing Production Coordinator (collateral), Master Data Analyst (event evidence), Finance Manager, Legal (fee-schedule enforceability), Supplier
Source: workflow W5510 — Supplier Service-Fee Billing &amp; Account Deduction for Store-Rendered Services (Barcode Labels &amp; Promotional Collaterals)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5510_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5510_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5510_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5510_Lane3" name="Store Ops Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5510_Lane4" name="AP Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5510_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5510_Start6" name="(a) Chargeable service event auto-logged at source — barcode/price-label print run…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5510_Task7" name="Fee-schedule &amp; service-catalog setup at vendor contracting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fee-schedule &amp; service-catalog setup at vendor contracting: Category Manager and Legal record a versioned, effective-dated service-fee schedule on the trade agreement record (W688) with a vendor opt-in flag: free allowances (e.g., 50 barcode/price labels per new item at onboarding; 1 price-change re-label per item per quarter; standard shelf-edge label stock) and per-event fees (barcode/price label per tag; promotional collateral per piece by format; expedited same-week production surcharge; custom artwork/plate at cost + margin; source-tag re-application per tag; barcode change per SKU). The opt-in flag gates charging — events for non-enrolled vendors route to the Category Manager to absorb under co-op funding (W513) or decline the service. Schedule changes only at agreement renewal
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: ~1 hr/enrolled vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5510_Task8" name="Event capture at source (no manual billing entry)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Event capture at source (no manual billing entry): every chargeable event auto-logs with evidence — label print runs from print management (W4490/W181 print-run count, SKU, store); vendor-initiated barcode changes from Auto-ID change control (W4488); collateral production from the campaign work order (W1796/W1798 proof-of-performance, format, quantity); source-tag re-application from receipt-verification exceptions (W4498). Events are provisional until the underlying service completes (rejected artwork, unreached label, cancelled campaign log no fee). Co-op coverage check: events tied to a campaign carrying vendor co-op funding bill the co-op settlement path (W1799) instead and are excluded here — the event log carries the coverage flag as the double-recovery guard
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5510_Task9" name="Monthly aggregation &amp; statement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly aggregation &amp; statement: system aggregates finalized events by vendor into a monthly Supplier Service-Fee statement itemized by event type with evidence links (print-run IDs, campaign IDs, approval IDs) and free-allowance consumption per line so the vendor sees its remaining balance; gross fee, output VAT, and net lines shown separately; released to the vendor portal (W705)
Responsible (R): System / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: +10–15 min/vendor-month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5510_Task10" name="Statement review &amp; dispute window">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Statement review &amp; dispute window: 5 business days between portal release and posting; disputes raised in-portal route Store Operations first (operational facts — did the print run / production happen), then Category Manager (commercial), then Finance (rate/application); unresolved contested lines are withheld from posting (not auto-credited) and escalate per the W244 dispute path; an active unresolved dispute suspends that supplier&#x27;s expedited-service privilege
Responsible (R): Store Ops Manager / Category Manager / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: ~20 min/dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5510_Task11" name="Debit-memo posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Debit-memo posting: uncontested (or window-expired) statements post as AP debit memos per W770 with deduction type &quot;service fee&quot;, referencing the statement; system posts Dr. Accounts Payable — Vendor / Cr. Service Fee Revenue (contra print &amp; collateral cost) and Cr. Output VAT Payable; BIR service invoice issued per the e-invoicing path (W473) with 10-year evidence retention; one-to-one guard blocks double-deduction if the vendor also issues a credit note for the same events
Responsible (R): System / AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 5 min/statement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5510_Task12" name="Settlement netting &amp; exceptions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Settlement netting &amp; exceptions: debit memos auto-apply as deductions at the next W556 payment run; if the vendor has no open AP balance (consignment-only, prepaid, seasonal supplier), the system falls back to an AR service invoice collected per W8/W108; where the vendor requires a BIR 2307 creditable-withholding certificate on service payments, Finance offers the cash-settlement route — netting produces no payment against which a 2307 can be issued
Responsible (R): System / AP Accountant
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: 5 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5510_Task13" name="Reconciliation, analytics &amp; recovery review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Reconciliation, analytics &amp; recovery review: monthly W100 vendor statement reconciliation carries service-fee debit memos as a reconciling class; quarterly review compares fee income by event type against actual cost (W4489 label consumables &amp; print amortization, store labor minutes per W181, collateral production cost); persistent under-recovery triggers a fee-schedule change at renewal — never mid-term; results feed the vendor scorecard (VS-67) as service-usage information only, distinct from compliance penalties (W245)
Responsible (R): AP Accountant / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hrs/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5510_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5510_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5510_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5510_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-284 (ensure controlled execution — Invoice Processing &amp; Matching (PA-15.1).) | - operational: signed fee-schedule (vendor opt-in flag) required before any event becomes chargeable; provisional-event reversal before statement posting; dispute window precedes debit-memo posting; one-to-one debit-memo/credit-note matching
Owner: AP Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5510_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5510_Annotation15" targetRef="W5510_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5510_Flow17" sourceRef="W5510_Start6" targetRef="W5510_Task7" />
